## 🐛 Bug Report

When trying to format the value and applying the state, the text in text input is flickering:

![rn-input-flickering mov](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/3187772/56655200-81185c00-6668-11e9-89ae-fcd0f540de37.gif)

Any tips to prevent this behavior without the need to change the native code?

## To Reproduce
Using the code sample:

- Tap the text input
- Type `A`
- Type `1` repetitively 

## Expected Behavior

The text input should not display the invalid character.

## Code Example
```js
import React from 'react';
import { StyleSheet, Text, View, TextInput } from 'react-native';

export default class App extends React.Component {
  state = {
    text: ''
  }

  render() {
    return (
      <View style={styles.container}>
        <TextInput
          value={this.state.text}
          onChangeText={text => {
            
            text = text.replace(/[0-9]/g, '')

            this.setState({
              text
            })
          }}
          style={styles.input}
        />
      </View>
    );
  }
}

const styles = StyleSheet.create({
  container: {
    flex: 1,
    backgroundColor: '#fff',
    alignItems: 'center',
    justifyContent: 'center',
  },
  input: {
    width: '90%',
    height: 50,
    borderColor: 'gray',
    borderWidth: 1
  }
});
```

